{
  "_comment": [
    "Aster Futures V3 EIP-712 signature vectors for the nautilus-aster adapter.",
    "",
    "param_string values are copied verbatim from CCXT's static request fixtures",
    "(https://github.com/ccxt/ccxt, ts/src/test/static/request/aster.json), together with the",
    "test-only private key published in that same file. CCXT lists `signature` and `nonce` in",
    "its `skipKeys`, so the signatures recorded there are never verified by CCXT's own tests and",
    "no longer correspond to the recorded parameter strings. The expected signatures below were",
    "therefore regenerated with eth-account 0.14.0 -- the exact library used by Aster's own",
    "signing example at https://asterdex.github.io/aster-api-website/futures-v3/general-info/",
    "(encode_typed_data + Account.sign_message over the AsterSignTransaction domain).",
    "",
    "Note: `builder` and `feeRate` appear in some CCXT parameter strings because CCXT attaches",
    "its own builder-fee attribution. This adapter never sends those parameters; they are kept",
    "here only so the vectors stay byte-identical to the recorded fixtures."
  ],
